# Branch flow (metrohub-delivery)

**Agent work** (commits, pushes, agent-implemented fixes) is made on a **per-task ephemeral `claude/<name>` branch**, then pushed and PR'd straight to **`feature/wip`**. Do **not** commit or push implementation work directly to **`main`**, **`develop`**, or **`feature/wip`**. (The retired shared **`users/sunil/wip`** funnel is not used here — this repo uses the `claude/<name>` model, matching the other MetroHub repos and `dp-shop`.)

**Promotion ladder** (toward `main`, each step by **pull request** only):

```text
main  ←  develop  ←  feature/wip  ←  claude/<name>
```

- Before opening the stage-1 PR from **`claude/<name>`**, run **`git fetch origin`**, then merge **`origin/feature/wip`**, **`origin/develop`**, and **`origin/main`** into **`claude/<name>`** in that order; resolve conflicts at each step. Inbound sync only — never merge `claude/<name>` outward.
- Open the stage-1 PR **`claude/<name>` → `feature/wip`**; do **not** target `develop` or `main` from `claude/<name>`.
- **Keep `claude/<name>` until the change fully promotes**; delete the branch (local + origin) only after it lands at its final target.

**Promotion up the ladder — `feature/wip → develop → main` (settled 2026-07-28).** A **separate flow** from the stage-1 dev lane above; promotion review fixes land **directly on the promote branch** (this replaces the older "fresh `claude/<name>` reflow" for promotions). Promotions merge as **merge commits, never squash**.

- **Stage 1 (`feature/wip → develop`):** branch **`promote/wip-*`** off `feature/wip`; PR `promote/wip-* → develop`; fix all bot comments **directly on `promote/wip-*`**; merge into `develop`.
- **Stage 2 (`develop → main`):** branch **`promote/develop-*`** off `develop`; PR `promote/develop-* → main`; fix directly on `promote/develop-*`; merge into `main`.
- **Stage 3 (reconcile):** branch **`claude/*`** = merge of `main` + `develop` + `feature/wip`; PR **`claude/* → feature/wip`** so `feature/wip` catches up → `feature/wip == develop == main`. The **one sanctioned exception** to "never merge `develop`/`main` into a `feature/wip`-targeting branch".
- **Oversized promotions:** slice into range-based `promote/wip-*` branches (one per slice SHA), merge to `develop` in order; run **stages 2 & 3 once** after all slices land.

GitHub workflows are driven via the **`metrohub-gh-mcp`** MCP server, not the `gh` CLI.
